SDL_GPU Vulkan: give a resource over 2 MiB memory of its own size, not a 64 MiB block.

Upstream puts a resource up to SMALL_ALLOCATION_THRESHOLD (2 MiB) in shared 16 MiB blocks
and rounds a larger one up to LARGE_ALLOCATION_INCREMENT (64 MiB), whose rest later large
resources share. On a GPU with one memory type (Mali) a 2D app's screen, photograph, and
text atlas (34 MiB on the tablet) took a whole 64 MiB block, the largest tablet's two.

With this patch a large resource gets a VkDeviceMemory of exactly its memory requirements'
size, as transfer buffers (`dedicated`) already did, and such allocations are kept out of
the free list, so nothing else is placed in one and it is freed at a submit soon after its
resource is released. Small resources are unchanged. Exact rather than rounded to 4 or
8 MiB: the same allocation count, no waste, and SDL makes a resource's replacement before
releasing it, so a kept block would not be reused. Make large resources at load or on a
resize, not per frame: each is one vkAllocateMemory and one vkFreeMemory.

Draughts: docs/architecture/rendering.md (GPU memory), docs/goose-findings.md.

--- a/src/gpu/vulkan/SDL_gpu_vulkan.c	2026-11-08 20:45:40
+++ b/src/gpu/vulkan/SDL_gpu_vulkan.c	2026-11-08 20:45:40
@@ -1967,6 +1967,7 @@
     VkDeviceSize alignedOffset = 0;
     VkDeviceSize newRegionSize, newRegionOffset;
     Uint8 isHostVisible, smallAllocation, allocationResult;
+    bool exact;
     Sint32 i;
 
     isHostVisible =
@@ -1976,6 +1977,10 @@
     allocator = &renderer->memoryAllocator->subAllocators[memoryTypeIndex];
     requiredSize = memoryRequirements->size;
     smallAllocation = requiredSize <= SMALL_ALLOCATION_THRESHOLD;
+    /* Patched: a large resource gets memory of its own size, as a dedicated one does, rather
+       than a block rounded up to LARGE_ALLOCATION_INCREMENT that later large resources share.
+       On a GPU with one memory type a few window-sized textures took a second 64 MiB block. */
+    exact = dedicated || !smallAllocation;
 
     if ((buffer == VK_NULL_HANDLE && image == VK_NULL_HANDLE) ||
         (buffer != VK_NULL_HANDLE && image != VK_NULL_HANDLE)) {
@@ -1987,7 +1992,7 @@
 
     selectedRegion = NULL;
 
-    if (dedicated) {
+    if (exact) {
         // Force an allocation
         allocationSize = requiredSize;
     } else {
@@ -2085,13 +2090,7 @@
             VULKAN_INTERNAL_MarkAllocationsForDefrag(renderer);
         }
 
-        if (requiredSize > SMALL_ALLOCATION_THRESHOLD) {
-            // allocate a page of required size aligned to LARGE_ALLOCATION_INCREMENT increments
-            allocationSize =
-                VULKAN_INTERNAL_NextHighestAlignment(requiredSize, LARGE_ALLOCATION_INCREMENT);
-        } else {
-            allocationSize = SMALL_ALLOCATION_SIZE;
-        }
+        allocationSize = SMALL_ALLOCATION_SIZE;
     }
 
     allocationResult = VULKAN_INTERNAL_AllocateMemory(
@@ -2133,6 +2132,13 @@
             allocation,
             newRegionOffset,
             newRegionSize);
+    }
+
+    /* Patched: keep a resource's own memory out of the free list, so that once released
+       nothing else is placed in it (one of exactly 16 MiB would pass for a small block) and
+       it goes back to the driver at a later submit, as any empty allocation does. */
+    if (exact) {
+        allocation->availableForAllocation = 0;
     }
 
     SDL_UnlockMutex(renderer->allocatorLock);
